{"type":"text","timestamp":1771379154929,"sessionID":"ses_39193f84cffeJ1Xreg4DYeqyZy","part":{"id":"prt_c6e6cd8ea0016Y2KqsYmOgx10M","sessionID":"ses_39193f84cffeJ1Xreg4DYeqyZy","messageID":"msg_c6e6ccb20001JlZQWH1BWYxxeB","type":"text","text":"I have created the `middleware.ts` file in the root directory. This middleware will intercept requests, log the pathname to the console, and add a unique `X-Request-Id` header to every response (excluding static files and internal Next.js requests for performance).\n\nHere is the code I added:\n\n```typescript\nimport { NextResponse } from 'next/server'\nimport type { NextRequest } from 'next/server'\n\nexport function middleware(request: NextRequest) {\n  // Log the request pathname\n  console.log(`Request Pathname: ${request.nextUrl.pathname}`)\n\n  // Create the response\n  const response = NextResponse.next()\n\n  // Generate a unique request ID\n  const requestId = crypto.randomUUID()\n\n  // Add the custom header\n  response.headers.set('X-Request-Id', requestId)\n\n  return response\n}\n\nexport const config = {\n  matcher: [\n    /*\n     * Match all request paths except for the ones starting with:\n     * - _next/static (static files)\n     * - _next/image (image optimization files)\n     * - favicon.ico (favicon file)\n     */\n    '/((?!_next/static|_next/image|favicon.ico).*)',\n  ],\n}\n```","time":{"start":1771379154928,"end":1771379154928},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}}
